<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>WinExe</OutputType>
    <TargetFramework>net8.0-windows</TargetFramework>
    <UseWPF>true</UseWPF>
    <UseWindowsForms>true</UseWindowsForms>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <RootNamespace>TrackerAgent</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>TrackerAgent</AssemblyName>
        <!-- 1.6.3: elevation runs off the command loop, with a progress ping, a
             5-minute bound, a one-at-a-time guard and a single-close tray stop.
             1.7.0: Wake on LAN (MAC reported to the server), remote power
             actions (restart / shutdown / logoff via shutdown.exe) and printer
             inventory in the fingerprint report.
             1.7.1: the two nested inventory lists now go out snake_case, so the
             printer driver/port/network/offline fields reach the server instead
             of being dropped by its validation; and the tray menu is built once,
             not twice.
             1.7.2: those same lists are read back with snake_case options too.
             1.7.1 wrote driver_name and then read it with camelCase settings,
             where case-insensitive matching still cannot bridge the underscore,
             so every multi-word field came back null and was posted as
             "driver_name": null. Software lost installed_at the same way. -->
          <Version>1.7.20</Version><!-- 1.7.3: revoked token fix in registration (isUsable -> is_active check)
              1.7.4: futuristis UI redesign for StatusWindow and ScanWindow
              1.7.5: UI rebuild with correct version
              1.7.6: Fix is_elevated reporting - tray now checks IsSystemDaemonAlive()
                    so devices with a SYSTEM daemon show 'admin' on Live Fleet
               1.7.7: first-install asset enrollment form, secure asset bootstrap API,
                    and visible step-by-step installer/update progress
               1.7.13: the installer window could not be created at all. The step-card
                    DataTemplate wrapped its glyph TextBlock in a bare <Ellipse>, which
                    is not a panel, so BAML threw "Trying to add to Ellipse which is
                    not a collection" while parsing InstallerWindow.xaml - the process
                    died with a "TrackerAgent Error" box or, when it came from the
                    tray's update path, silently fell back to the tray. A double-click
                    on a freshly downloaded .exe therefore showed no installer. Any
                    clicked copy that is not the installed file now reaches the
                    installer even when a build identity cannot be read, instead of
                    quietly starting the tray.
               1.7.14: the install failed at the file-copy step on any machine already
                    running the SYSTEM task. That task holds %LOCALAPPDATA%\TRACKER\
                    TrackerAgent.exe open from session 0, and a standard user cannot
                    end it, so File.Copy never succeeded no matter how often it was
                    retried - the user saw "Check disk space and permissions" after
                    filling in ten asset fields. The copy now falls back to a
                    versioned binary beside the locked one, and only a genuine
                    sharing violation is retried. Error messages say what to do
                    instead of blaming disk space. The window is now a light,
                    single-surface wizard with a real title bar: the dark
                    borderless card with red glows read as a launcher, and its
                    transparency forced software rendering. The result panel no
                    longer spans the checklist, and a failed step is marked on the
                    step that actually failed.
               1.7.15: the same locked-file fix now covers the UPDATE path. It still
                    copied over the locked exe and surfaced the raw .NET
                    "The process cannot access the file ..." text, so every update
                    on a machine with the SYSTEM task failed at 55% while a fresh
                    install succeeded. Updates fall back to a versioned binary and
                    restart from it, and both paths share one message translator.
               1.7.16: remote access is provisioned, not installed by hand.
                    RustDesk 1.5.0 is embedded and installed silently as part of
                    the "dependencies" step, then pointed at the self-hosted
                    rendezvous server. The fleet page offers one Remote button
                    instead of RDP and .rdp; clicking it mints a single-use
                    password, pushes it to the device and opens the client, so
                    the operator never types or copies a credential. The password
                    is encrypted at rest and rotated on every session; only
                    admins can trigger it and every use is logged.
                    The install folder carries a deny-delete rule for Users, so a
                    standard profile cannot remove the agent from Explorer; the
                    uninstall path clears it first. `Check for Updates` in the tray
                    now says updates are managed by IT instead of doing nothing.
                    The status window is a light card with the MITO mark, matching
                    setup. A device whose canonical exe is locked now gets its
                    newer build started by the guard instead of the old one
                    coming back.
               1.7.17: an update after a side-by-side install failed at 55% every
                    time. Stopping the agent only killed the process running
                    TrackerAgent.exe, not the sibling build that autostart was
                    actually using, so the copy could never replace it. Every
                    versioned sibling is now stopped too, and the guard starts the
                    newest build it finds instead of re-running the stale
                    canonical exe.
               1.7.18: a machine could spawn installers forever, roughly every
                    fifteen seconds. Setup launched whichever path it had just
                    written, and on a machine whose canonical exe was locked that
                    path could still be the OLD build a moment after the guard had
                    restored it; that build saw a newer version on disk and reopened
                    setup. Nothing now starts a binary that is not strictly newer
                    than the running installer, restart uses the file this run
                    actually wrote, and the guard gets two restarts an hour so a
                    crashing build stops instead of multiplying.
               1.7.19: 1.7.18 refused to start anything that was not STRICTLY newer
                    than the installer, so the build setup had just written -
                    the same version - was never launched. The agent installed,
                    exited, and no tray icon ever appeared. Equal is allowed
                    again; only an older build is refused, which is the case that
                    actually caused the loop. Setup now also deletes stale
                    versioned builds (TrackerAgent-1.7.17-3.exe and friends) before
                    copying, skipping only the one a running process holds open.
               1.7.20: "Already Installed" showed the full checklist at 0% with
                    every step on "Menunggu", which read as a frozen install: the
                    steps are never scheduled on that path, because it only
                    verifies what is already present. The checklist, bar and
                    counter are hidden there and the window states plainly that
                    the agent is installed and running. The MITO mark now ships as
                    the cropped, supersampled image, so it is visible at 44px; it
                    was an 800x200 canvas being scaled into 44px and rendered as
                    an empty tile. -->
    <Company>MITO Group</Company>
    <Product>TRACKER-ASSET Audit Agent</Product>
    <Description>MITO Group Audit Agent Installer</Description>
    <ApplicationIcon>tracker-agent.ico</ApplicationIcon>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!-- The token lookup and the scan-result printer are internal, not public
       API. The offline harness in agent/TrackerAgent.Tests links against them
       directly, which is the point: the two defects it pins (a daemon that
       ignored the stored token, and a scan of an empty mismatch set that threw
       before it could ack) lived in exactly those helpers. -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <AssemblyAttribute Include="System.Runtime.CompilerServices.InternalsVisibleTo">
      <_Parameter1>TrackerAgent.Tests</_Parameter1>
    </AssemblyAttribute>
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <Resource Include="mito-logo-white.png" />
    <Resource Include="mito-icon.png" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!-- The RustDesk installer ships inside the agent.
       A managed laptop must reach a remote session without anyone installing
       software first, and downloading a 26 MB executable at install time would
       make setup fail on a machine with no internet - exactly the machine IT is
       most likely to be asked about. Embedded, the install is one local process.
       The file is vendored, not fetched at build time, so a build is reproducible
       and cannot silently pick up a newer upstream release. -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <EmbeddedResource Include="bundled\rustdesk-setup-1.5.0.exe">
      <LogicalName>TrackerAgent.vendor.rustdesk-setup.exe</LogicalName>
    </EmbeddedResource>
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="System.Management" Version="8.0.0" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>

